enchilada: kernel reboots and panics reset into fastboot (PON reboot reason)

A kernel restart did nothing on this port: PE_halt_restart was NULL, so PEHaltRestart() returned
-1 and halt_all_cpus() spun (osfmk/arm64/machine_routines.c), and a panic ended in
panic_spin_forever() (debug=0xc sets panicDebugging). A reset that does happen (PSCI
SYSTEM_RESET from the shim, a long Power press) boots Android from boot_a. The SDM845 ABL takes
the reboot reason from the PMIC: PON SOFT_RB_SPARE (PM8998 SID 0, 0x88f), bits 7:1, 0x02 =
bootloader (Linux qcom-pon "qcom,pm8998-pon", pm8998.dtsi mode-bootloader = <0x2>, made for
Pixel 3 / DB845; downstream qpnp_pon_set_restart_reason()). IMEM restart_reason = 0x77665500
alone did not work (the shim wrote it and still landed in Android); it is written too.
SweetPlatformExpert now sets PE_halt_restart: kPERestartCPU and kPEPanicRestartCPU go to
sweet_reboot_fastboot() in sweet_spmi.c, which holds the keys thread (it polls PON on the same
observer channel), read-modify-writes only bits 7:1 of SOFT_RB_SPARE through the PON APID's RW
channel (chnls 0x0c600000 + 0x10000 * APID, EXT_WRITEL as in spmi-pmic-arb.c v5; mapped at boot
only if the arbiter says the APID belongs to EE 0 and PON_SUBTYPE reads GEN2_PRIMARY), reads it
back, writes IMEM, logs "SWEET RB: restart -> fastboot (pon spare 0x.., imem 0x..)" and issues
PSCI SYSTEM_RESET. If the spare register does not read back as bootloader there is no reset (an
unmarked reset boots Android, which would reformat userdata): the old spin. panic_spin_forever()
first keeps the panic screen pfb seconds (default 60, spin delays with interrupts off), then
does the same. Boot logs "SWEET RB: boot with pon spare ..." (what the last reset left).
Boot-args: rbfb=0 = reboots do nothing as before; pfb=N seconds, pfb=0 = panic screen forever.

